+## Optional pump-aware PWM coordination
+
+Pump-aware PWM groups coordinate already-earned HEAT pulses sharing a circulation
+pump. They are disabled by default. `minimal` reduces interruptions by chaining
+pulses; `maximal` concentrates their energized window. These are separate goals:
+neither strategy guarantees fewer starts, shorter runtime or lower energy in
+every load profile. Hydraulic weights prefer solo time for larger zones while
+minimum times, deferral, priority and restart accounting remain authoritative.
+
+PWM restart journals use the compact `adaptive_climate_pwm_coordination` HA Store.
+Migration persists the new journal before marking the learning Store; original
+learning data are retained. Safety-critical writes remain awaited. After migration,
+a missing dedicated journal blocks coordinated ON instead of restoring stale data.
+Back up before upgrade; safely stop groups before rolling back to code that cannot
+read the new journal. Do not delete the migration marker as a recovery shortcut.
+
+The existing `pwm_coordination` diagnostics include Hydraulic Consistency, solo
+time, competing load, pulse variation and coverage. HC describes the variability
+of relative competing hydraulic weight; stable solo operation and stable overlap
+can both score 100. It is not measured flow, physical valve position or proof of
+better learning. Collection resets on restart. Optional Template sensors and
+ApexCharts examples use Recorder/InfluxDB without a second critical journal.
+
+See the repository documentation for configuration, supported topology, exact
+formulas, CSV history analysis, genuine rolling 24h/7d evaluation, test plans and
+measured synthetic benchmarks:
